    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316-a1">

                <pb facs="0777" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg693"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">note.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Matamoros</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-07"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 7,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consul Brigham is a lawyer, has been a judge, and is a man of much ability and
                    experience. I fully concur in what he says in this case as to the Mexican courts
                    in general. A reading of my reports on previous cases will show that 1 have said
                    substantially the same things over and over again. With this comment I submit
                    the case to the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed>WARNER P. SUTTON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
